From 0deb8e82fe6ceb49bd5bcf5268c6aa7124dc6939 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GGEZUS <coelho.b.ricardo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 20:32:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] feat(input): discrete 4-finger vertical swipe gestures

A vertical swipe recognized with four or more fingers now runs a
configurable action instead of driving the workspace carousel:

    touchscreen-swipe {
        swipe-4-down { close-window; }
        swipe-4-up   { spawn-sh "wvkbd-deskintl -H 260"; }
    }

The action fires when the fingers lift; the grab swallows events for
the rest of the gesture. When unset, 4-finger vertical swipes keep the
carousel behavior. GestureEvent::Begin now reports the tracked finger
count.

Also: revert the vertical swipe to the original (touchpad-natural)
direction after trying both on hardware.
---
